        "comparison": "Both Microsoft (MU) and Broadcom (AVGO) address the infrastructure demands of AI and high-performance computing (HPC), but they focus on different layers of the stack. MU’s HBM disclosure details the memory component technology (3D stacked DRAM with through-silicon vias) that enables high bandwidth and energy efficiency, which is critical for AI workloads. In contrast, AVGO’s custom silicon (ASIC) disclosure focuses on the processing and integration layer, providing IP platforms to design ASICs that integrate embedded logic and memory to target AI and HPC applications. While MU provides the high-bandwidth memory subsystem, AVGO provides the custom processor/platform architecture that leverages such components for specific AI/HPC tasks.",
